lisa-design:
- Merge logic extracted from cmd/ccf-bump/merge.go into internal/automerge (Merger with Label/BranchPrefix/Author/Commits) rather than flags on `ccf-bump merge`: ccf-bump's repo selection requires release: true, but Renovate's shard includes release:false repos (workflows, the templates). ccf-bump's merge tests pass unchanged (its messages are identical: BranchPrefix "ccf-bump/" renders "ccf-bump/*").
- `renovate-config merge` requires --repos (the run's shard = the token's scope) and does not shard again; --dry-run reuses renovate-config's values (off merges, any other value prints), defaulting to a dry run.
- Renovate's isBranchModified equivalent: every commit of the PR (pulls/N/commits, up to 250) must be authored by --author; zero commits or an unlinked author ("") leaves the PR. Evidence: Renovate's commits with the app token are API commits authored by ccf-release-bot[bot] (workflows#123 head 094c1a5, verified).
- The renovate:automerge label is a separate packageRule (negation-only matchPackageNames excluding OPA's three names, non-major update types), not on the non-major group rule: Renovate unions addLabels across rules (mergeable), so a later rule can't remove it, and adding OPA negations to the group rule would change OPA's automerge outside the api. Validator rejects "*" combined with negations, so the rule uses negations only. Never in vulnerabilityAlerts (force replaces addLabels).
- renovate.yml: second app token minted after the Renovate step (same shard, guarded on steps.select success and non-empty repos so it is never unscoped), merge step `--wait 20m` with timeout 25; Renovate step gets timeout 55 (token hour); job timeout 60 -> 90.

